{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 129, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing the direct input-output edge when edge 4 is also absent cuts most paths to the output, causing much larger drops (exps 4, 6 vs 1)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 absent, deleting edge 5 leaves only the direct skip (or nothing) to the output, collapsing accuracy (exps 63, 64 vs 61)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct edge 0->3, edge 5 is a key path to the output so removing it hurts more (exps 62, 64 vs 61)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Dropping a skip on edge 5 loses little capacity compared with dropping a 3x3 conv, and can even help skip-heavy cells (exps 65, 67 vs 61)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing a parameter-free skip on edge 0 costs less than removing a 3x3 conv (exp 97 vs 96)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty direct edge adds a new path to the output instead of replacing a useful skip or conv (exps 71, 75-79 vs 72-74)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the direct input-output skip is missing, a skip on edge 4 restores residual-like gradient flow (exp 34 vs 31-33)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 1 supplies identity information that the cell lacks when edge 3 is none (exps 57, 58 vs 51-56)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "